WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.230
Our VFFs, who chose today's book,

2
00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:05.240
are three incredible high school students

3
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:08.260
who helped launch a groundbreaking magazine.

4
00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:10.210
I've had it on my desk for the last few months.

5
00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.220
It's called Pass the Spatula

6
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:16.080
which celebrates trailblazing chefs of color.

7
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:16.913
Take a look.

8
00:00:18.036 --> 00:00:21.000 line:15%
My name is Chayil and I'm 18 years old.

9
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.676 line:15%
I am the Co-creative Director of Pass the Spatula magazine.

10
00:00:23.676 --> 00:00:26.650 line:15%
My name is Anthony and I am 18 years old.

11
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.580 line:15%
I am the Marketing, PR

12
00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:30.910 line:15%
and social media manager for the magazine.

13
00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:33.560 line:15%
Hello. My name is Chris and I am 17 years old.

14
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:35.600 line:15%
I was a Recipe Developer and Interviewer

15
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:36.810 line:15%
for Pass the Spatula.

16
00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:38.190
I go to Food and Finance High School

17
00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:40.390
and my peers and I helped to create

18
00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:42.100
Pass the Spatula Magazine last year.

19
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.491
Pass the Spatula is a spin on, Pass the Light.

20
00:00:44.491 --> 00:00:45.660
It's a student run magazine

21
00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.520
created to highlight past, present

22
00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.780
and future chefs of color.

23
00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:52.540
Often times, chefs of color usually go unrecognized

24
00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:55.250
and we wanted to do our best to uplift them.

25
00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:57.250
We honor these chefs of color in different ways

26
00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:59.890
by showing recipes, by showing their stories

27
00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:01.980
and showcasing what they've done in the past

28
00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:03.930
and how we can move on from that in the future.

29
00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.680
My main goal is to just bring the message

30
00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:08.720
of Pass the Spatula throughout the world.

31
00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.460
This is all something that we're passionate about.

32
00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.060
Even as high school students, we can have an impact.

33
00:01:14.472 --> 00:01:16.613
(applause)

34
00:01:16.613 --> 00:01:18.960
It's a very well done magazine.

35
00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:23.597
Please welcome, Chayil, Anthony and Chris. (cheers)

36
00:01:23.597 --> 00:01:26.482
(applause)

37
00:01:26.482 --> 00:01:27.430
I'm so geeking out.

38
00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:29.870
I've literally been such a lover of your magazine.

39
00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:31.130
I can't believe I'm meeting you.

40
00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:33.570
It is such a huge accomplishment.

41
00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:34.850
What you guys have made.

42
00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:37.786
What have each of you personally learned

43
00:01:37.786 --> 00:01:39.550
from this experience?

44
00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:41.800
Chayil, I'd love to start with you.

45
00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:44.863
Yeah. So for me, I know this experience has been, you know

46
00:01:44.863 --> 00:01:47.661
a really good eye-opener and I know for me,

47
00:01:47.661 --> 00:01:49.407
you kind of look at this experience and say,

48
00:01:49.407 --> 00:01:50.480
"I have a voice," you know,

49
00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.080
it's not just someone who has a degree,

50
00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:53.220
someone who has a title.

51
00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:55.310
Even if it's just like something small that you've written.

52
00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:56.780
I didn't write like a whole, you know,

53
00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:57.630
bunch in the magazine

54
00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:59.860
but even that small little blurb I've written,

55
00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:02.410
even that I'm small little drawing that I did.

56
00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:04.760
I know it has an impact on somebody's life.

57
00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:05.780
It really does.

58
00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:09.236
And Anthony, how has it been for you?

59
00:02:09.236 --> 00:02:12.930
Yeah. This experience has been really incredible.

60
00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:15.210
I mean, you know, going into this magazine

61
00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:18.010
we honestly didn't know what a magazine

62
00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:19.760
was supposed to be like. We didn't know what the process

63
00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.970
of creating a magazine was.

64
00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:24.950
So by going into this magazine,

65
00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:26.610
we were exposed to such a plethora

66
00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:28.270
of different opportunities

67
00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:31.110
and really it just opened up the possibilities

68
00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:33.420
of food for me and my future career.

69
00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.773
Chris, how has it been for you?

70
00:02:35.773 --> 00:02:38.170 line:15%
So this magazine shows that anything could happen

71
00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.770 line:15%
especially during a pandemic.

72
00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:42.750 line:15%
On top of that, we had the great message to show

73
00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:44.470 line:15%
that black chefs do matter

74
00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:47.230
and do need a voice and especially the spotlight.

75
00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:48.940 line:15%
So especially, it was definitely great

76
00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:50.880 line:15%
especially during these trying times.

77
00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:54.030 line:15%
Well, I agree completely

78
00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:57.440
and I just love the cookbook

79
00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.010
that you picked for today's club.

80
00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:04.508
It's Mix-tape Pot-Luck by Quest Love.

81
00:03:04.508 --> 00:03:07.530
I have to tell you, I am his biggest fan

82
00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:11.130
and this book is set up like a dinner party.

83
00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:13.320
Are you guys a fan of this format?

84
00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:16.180
Why did you bring it to the club, Chayil?

85
00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:17.210
Yes, definitely.

86
00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:19.270
I know for me, you know, when you go through cookbooks

87
00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:20.660
it's probably like, all soups

88
00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:23.350
or like, all salmon, like, okay, I love me a good soup

89
00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:25.040
but I want to get a little bit of everything.

90
00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:26.410
Like I want to get an appetizer,

91
00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:29.760
an entree, a dessert and everything is in this book.

92
00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:30.940
It's something that, you know,

93
00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.921
you can see things that you've never seen before.

94
00:03:33.921 --> 00:03:35.370
And another thing I love about this book

95
00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:37.300
is that there's music to pair along with it.

96
00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:40.530
So good food, good tunes is a great experience.

97
00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:41.410
It's just amazing.

98
00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:44.270
You can't have a dinner party without music.

99
00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:45.591
It would be blasphemy.

100
00:03:45.591 --> 00:03:46.819
(laughing)

101
00:03:46.819 --> 00:03:47.840
And I love getting the opportunity

102
00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:50.310
to learn from these talented chefs.

103
00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:54.270
And one of the chefs in the cookbook is Kwame Onwuachi.

104
00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:57.560
And you also featured him on Pass the Spatula.

105
00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.301
And Chris, you wrote an article

106
00:03:59.301 --> 00:04:01.260
and a recipe inspired by him.

107
00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:03.440
Why is he such a role model for you?

108
00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.270
Oh, from his upbringing to where he is now,

109
00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:07.470
which has head chef. It definitely shows that

110
00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:09.530
anything can come true with hard work

111
00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:11.270
and being able to being able to know,

112
00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.963
interview him and create the jollof rice with jerk chicken,

113
00:04:13.963 --> 00:04:18.270
definitely encapsulates who he is as a person.

114
00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:22.750
I have been such a Kwame fan for so long

115
00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:26.210
cause I haven't missed one frame of top chef.

116
00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:28.793
(upbeat music)

